  "_comment": [
    "Behavioral model for the poisoned_mcp_tool_two_sessions divergence scenario:",
    "the interactive demo's two sessions. Session -update-001 asked the agent to",
    "update the project's dependencies and run the tests; while doing so the agent",
    "read the project's own .npmrc and .mcp.json (its scope claims them, inside its",
    "working directory). Session -read-001, started after it, asked for the release",
    "notes through the changelog tool and nothing else.",
    "",
    "run_divergence_detection.sh rewrites window_start / ingested_at to now,",
    "window_end to now + 20m, every 'demo_openclaw' token to the prefix of the",
    "--agent-type in use, and every '__STATE_DIR__' token to the trigger's state",
    "directory (the sessions' working directory). Each prediction's transcript",
    "span is rewritten from its '_span' offsets (seconds from the upsert):",
    "-update-001 ended three minutes before the upsert, -read-001 is still open.",
    "",
    "The trigger stages the project, the runner plants this model, then the tool",
    "call edits tests/test_access_control.py a second or two later: the write",
    "falls inside the read session's transcript span plus the file monitor's",
    "observation lag, so it is attributed to -read-001 by containment and never",
    "to -update-001 through the slack. The scenario asserts both, and that the",
    "update session's .npmrc / .mcp.json claims raise no scope_escalation."
  ],
